<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vibilius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vibilius was a king of the Hermunduri in the 1st century CE, known from the historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a>. In 19 CE he helped to overthrow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catualda">Catualda</a>, who had ousted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maroboduus">Maroboduus</a> as ruler of the Marcomanni, and around 50 CE, together with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lugii">Lugii</a>, he brought down <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vannius">Vannius</a>, king of the Quadi, while the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> stood aside.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vibilius.jpg" alt="Vibilius" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DaniDF1995 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GermanenAD50-it.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
